As part of the data migration process, the Nautilus DevOps team is actively creating several S3 buckets on AWS. 
They plan to utilize both private and public S3 buckets to store the relevant data. 
Given the ongoing migration of other infrastructure to AWS, it is logical to consolidate data storage within the AWS environment as well.

Create a public S3 bucket named devops-s3-591867430 using Terraform.

Ensure the bucket is accessible publicly once created by setting the proper ACL.

The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Notes:

Create the resources only in the us-east-1 region.
Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.
The name of the S3 bucket should be based on devops-s3-591867430.
You can use the ACL settings to ensure the bucket is publicly accessible.

SOLUTION

To create a public S3 bucket in your LocalStack environment, you need to define the bucket and then explicitly disable the public access block settings that AWS enables by default. 
The acl argument alone is not enough in modern Terraform; you must also configure aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block to allow public access.

Here is the main.tf to accomplish this:

hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "devops_bucket" {
  bucket = "devops-s3-591867430"

  tags = {
    Name = "devops-s3-591867430"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "devops_bucket_public_access" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.devops_bucket.id

  block_public_acls       = false
  block_public_policy     = false
  ignore_public_acls      = false
  restrict_public_buckets = false
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_acl" "devops_bucket_acl" {
  depends_on = [
    aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block.devops_bucket_public_access,
  ]

  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.devops_bucket.id
  acl    = "public-read"
}
💡 Key Details
Bucket Name: Set exactly to devops-s3-591867430 as required.

Public Access Block: The aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block resource is essential. 
By setting all four flags to false, you disable the default security settings that would otherwise block the public ACL .

ACL: The aws_s3_bucket_acl resource applies the public-read canned ACL. The depends_on ensures the public access block is configured first, preventing a race condition .

Region: Your provider.tf already sets the region to us-east-1, so no extra configuration is needed here.

🚀 Execution Steps
Run the following in the terminal inside /home/bob/terraform:

bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
⚠️ Note on LocalStack Validation
Some KodeKloud community posts mention that the task checker sometimes looks for the bucket in real AWS rather than LocalStack, causing false failures even when the bucket exists locally . If you encounter this, verify the bucket exists with:

bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 s3api head-bucket --bucket devops-s3-591867430
If the bucket exists locally, the Terraform configuration is correct.
